{"skill":{"slug":"elevenlabs-tts","displayName":"Elevenlabs Tts"},"version":{"version":"2.4.0","createdAt":1775035003031,"changelog":"Fix: Updated TTS file path from /tmp/tts-*/ to /tmp/openclaw/tts-*/. Added safety check to always use latest file. Added workspace copy step for message tool compatibility.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":11061,"sha256":"1303eba382720af8800586266e3eb2dcda88bfc5ad6e2e466b7718f3586e124f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/audio-tags.md","size":6750,"sha256":"cd8bf4cbb13d6e1e476766c24ee191dac314828ac27ec9269b2ec2f8e2dbbb6d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2203,"sha256":"caa7838c61702efdaf352aff7ad9ef0b9cc6dd1821e6110cdbcdb66d6718ec4f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031264174,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"58228ad4a28fb47b7172b24e9eb08b1bd60a8e4b621d98912288848e3afbecda","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/58228ad4a28fb47b7172b24e9eb08b1bd60a8e4b621d98912288848e3afbecda","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: elevenlabs-tts\nVersion: 2.4.0\n\nThe skill provides ElevenLabs TTS integration but relies on the agent executing shell commands via the 'exec' tool for file discovery, audio conversion with ffmpeg, and file management (cp, rm) as detailed in SKILL.md. While these actions are plausibly necessary for the stated goal of sending WhatsApp voice notes, the use of complex shell pipelines and hardcoded paths like '/root/.openclaw/workspace/' represents a high-risk capability that could be exploited for shell injection or unauthorized file access if the agent processes unsanitized user input.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161144879},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":46,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789031264174},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is mostly a normal ElevenLabs voice-message helper, but its documented WhatsApp workflow can pick and send the wrong temporary audio file.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using ElevenLabs, ffmpeg, tts, and message tools fits the stated purpose, but combining broad exec-based temporary-file discovery with external WhatsApp sending creates an avoidable content-substitution risk.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains markdown instructions and a reference file only; I found no bundled executable scripts, installer, service registration, or hidden install behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The WhatsApp workflow tells the agent to search broad predictable /tmp paths and choose the newest matching audio file before sending it, which is not reliably tied to the current TTS generation and conflicts with its own warning that old legacy files may exist.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifacts do not request persistence, background agents, privilege escalation, memory writes, or long-running services; the cleanup command deletes only the documented workspace copy.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The core purpose is coherent: it documents ElevenLabs text-to-speech, voice selection, audio tags, ffmpeg conversion, and sending generated audio through WhatsApp.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review the WhatsApp workflow before installing. Prefer a version that uses the exact output path from the current tts call or a private per-run directory, and do not let it send audio found by scanning shared /tmp locations. Treat text sent to ElevenLabs and WhatsApp recipients as external disclosure.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: the documented find/xargs/ls workflow can select stale or unrelated audio from shared temporary paths and then feed it into the WhatsApp send step.\n[TM1] expected: Downgraded: the rm command is a disclosed cleanup step for a specific temporary workspace audio file, not evidence of destructive or deceptive behavior.\n[E1] expected: Expected for an ElevenLabs TTS integration: user text and the configured API key are necessarily used with ElevenLabs, though users should avoid sensitive text unless they trust that provider.\n[SQP-3] expected: The fixed en languageCode example is a documentation limitation, not a security concern; the skill also includes multilingual examples and states multilingual support.\n[SDI-2] expected: The cp/rm and ffmpeg steps are purpose-aligned with preparing WhatsApp-compatible audio, but the surrounding file-selection workflow is the part that creates review-level concern.\n[SQP-2] expected: The cleanup deletion is narrow and disclosed, but the instructions would be safer with an explicit path-verification warning.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031264174}}}}}